  A CONSTANT slope and r ~ -1 means ln DeltaE = -n S~ + const, i.e.
  the tunnelling is exponential in the SPIN SIZE, exactly as a
  large-spin WKB predicts - and NOT of the form e^{-S0/h} with S0 a
  path integral over a fixed landscape.

  CONSEQUENCE FOR QLTO. The design/walk register at q=2 levels per
  parameter is a spin-n/2 system, not a discretised particle. Every
  continuum tunnelling bound quoted for it - including v99 PART 4's
  exp(width) vs exp(height) reading - is being applied outside its
  hypotheses. The CYCLE register (PART 5, slope -0.998) is a genuine
  particle-on-a-lattice and the bound does hold there.
